Z||000004||Patrick86GT||08-08-2001||05:56 PM||||I have 4 GT's, 2 88's & 2 86's. I'm about convinced that constant idle speed is nearly impossible to achieve for this backyard mechanic.  I settled for the 1000-1100 RPM, although it bugs me, too. 3 out of 4 of mine idle there (all manual tranny's) <P>But the automatic idles steady at 1100 and  , on rare occasion, will die at a stop in drive (restarts immediately)....I've changed all kinds of parts (O2 sensor, EGR, IAC) and cleaned the throttle body as well as a fresh tune up.  Of course, there are no codes!<P>I'm wondering what to do next.  ||||reg||1
